<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Collegium (Sweden)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The collegia were central administrative boards created in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> under the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axel-oxenstierna">Axel Oxenstierna</a>, responsible for finance, war, admiralty, justice and commerce. They were organised during the minority of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christina-queen-of-sweden">Queen Christina</a>. The system made the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>'s administration more systematic than that of most contemporary European states and influenced Peter I's reforms in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p></div>
